280 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (          After studying several methods of eliminating waste plastics, the IGNA team considered pyrolysis one of the most effective ways of processing plastics in recent world. Pyrolysis holds significant potential for waste management, renewable energy production and the generation of valuable chemicals. By converting waste plastic into valuable end products, pyrolysis offers a promising route for sustainable energy production and waste reduction. [10])
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
281 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (          Pyrolysis is a chemical process in which organic materials are decomposed at high temperatures in the absence of oxygen. This results in the breakdown of complex molecules into simpler compounds. One of the most valuable end products is pyrolysis oil what can be used as raw material for chemical industry. [11])
/Pg 15 0 R
>>
endobj
282 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Here's a general overview of how pyrolysis works to produce oil:)
/E (Here's a general overview of how pyrolysis works to produce oil:)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
283 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (1. Feedstock Preparation: Waste plastics are first prepared by shredding or chopping into smaller pieces to facilitate handling and improve heat transfer during pyrolysis.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E <>
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6 7]
>>
endobj
285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (3. Degradation and Vaporization: As the temperature increases, the organic molecules in the feedstock undergo thermal degradation, breaking down into smaller fragments. These fragments vaporize, releasing volatile gases and forming vapors containing a mixture of organic compounds.)
/Pg 15 0 R
>>
endobj
286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (4. Condensation: During pyrolysis, the vapors are processed through various catalysts and cooled, causing the heavier organic compounds to condense  into liquid fractions. These liquid fractions form the oil product.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
endobj
287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (5. Separation and Upgrading: The collected oil may undergo further processing steps, such as filtration, centrifugation, or chemical treatment, to remove impurities and upgrade its quality. This may involve removing water, acids, and other undesired compounds to improve the stability and energy content of the oil.)
/Pg 15 0 R
>>
endobj
288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (6. Utilization: The resulting oil can be used as a raw material in the chemical industry and can also be converted into new oil products. [12])
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [10]
>>
